# Build context for the dashboard image.
#
# The build context is `new_app/license_manager/` (see dashboard/Dockerfile), so
# every pattern here is matched against paths relative to THAT directory. A bare
# `node_modules` or `.next` would only match a directory directly under the
# context root and would therefore NOT exclude `dashboard/node_modules` — the
# mistake that produced a 785 MB context and, worse, merged the host dependency
# tree over the image's own `node_modules` during `COPY dashboard/ ./`.

# Start from "nothing", then re-admit only the dashboard application source.
*
!dashboard
!dashboard/**
*.md

# Host build output and dependencies: `npm ci` runs inside the image, and the
# standalone build is produced there too. Copying the host's copies both bloats
# the context and corrupts the image's node_modules (BuildKit must chmod files
# that belong to an immutable lower layer -> "read-only file system").
dashboard/node_modules
dashboard/.next
dashboard/out
dashboard/coverage
dashboard/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Tests and their tooling are not part of a production build.
dashboard/tests
dashboard/vitest.config.ts
dashboard/vitest.setup.ts

# Secrets and local configuration never enter a build context.
dashboard/.env
dashboard/.env.*
dashboard/*.pem
dashboard/*.key
**/application_default_credentials.json
**/*service-account*.json

# Local noise.
dashboard/*.log
dashboard/.DS_Store
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# The image is built from this file, not from a copy inside the context.
dashboard/Dockerfile
dashboard/.dockerignore
